# Docs and proof surfaces

This site is a **developer environment** (discover → retrieve → inspect → render), not a generic component gallery and not a marketing landing page. Borrow shadcn’s *proof + distribution* model; do **not** clone the ui.shadcn.com SaaS mosaic or Geist/zinc look.

Canonical IA and page anatomies remain in:

- [docs/TARGET_ARCHITECTURE.md](docs/TARGET_ARCHITECTURE.md)
- [docs/page-anatomy.md](docs/page-anatomy.md)
- [docs/product-architecture.md](docs/product-architecture.md)

This rule covers **how pages prove and teach**. Nav chrome follows **J6** in [docs/TARGET_ARCHITECTURE.md](docs/TARGET_ARCHITECTURE.md). If a change conflicts with frozen docs, record it for human review (or amend via an explicit decision).

## Homepage

Lead with **one short product thesis** (what this environment is: data → render → TfL visuals) and **one composed proof surface**.

- Prefer a **Block** (e.g. Week ahead) as the living proof — status + schematic strips, not finance/chat/QR widgets.
- Keep chrome quiet so TfL domain visuals carry the first viewport.
- **Catalog / index grids are secondary.** Do not make a multi-section catalog the emotional centre of `/`. Sidebar + section hubs already discover content.
- One primary CTA path is enough (hero-right **Browse components** / Installation). Proof demos on `/` are not clickable doc frames — do not wrap boards in overlay links.
- Avoid “Build Your Own” style theme playgrounds until Docs → Components → Blocks is solid.
- Arrivals proof boards follow fixed-tile rhythm: [docs/design-system.md](docs/design-system.md#arrivals-board-rhythm), [`.cursor/rules/arrivals-board-layout.mdc`](arrivals-board-layout.mdc).

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — thesis + Block proof, catalog demoted
<>
  <p>…one sentence thesis…</p>
  <WeekAheadSection />
  {/* optional short pointer; catalog not the hero */}
</>

// ❌ BAD — catalog-first or generic SaaS bento as brand
<>
  <DocsCatalogGrid />
  <FinanceDemoMosaic />
</>
```

## Blocks (compositions)

**Blocks** are mini-app / composition demos (human amendment J1). They sit outside the reusable atomic registry by default.

A Block page should teach composition, not pretend to be one installable atom:

1. **Purpose** — what composition story this shows  
2. **Preview** — full-bleed or wide live demo (primary)  
3. **Composition recipe** — which **Interfaces** + **Primitives** (+ Foundations) it uses, with links  
4. **Optional Code / file map** — how the composition is wired (Preview/Code pattern à la shadcn Blocks)  
5. **Not a dumping ground** — incomplete ideas stay in **Drafts** with a promotion path  

Do **not** invent a single registry JSON for an entire Block unless we deliberately ship a block package. Point consumers at the Interfaces/Primitives they should install instead.

## Interface and primitive docs

Follow [docs/page-anatomy.md](docs/page-anatomy.md). Page chrome may wrap sections; do not skip the conceptual order.

**Preview before prose.** `renderComponentDocs` already mounts Preview first when a demo exists. MDX body should stay example-first:

| Page type | Lead with | Then |
|-----------|-----------|------|
| Interface | Purpose → Preview → Install → **Getting the data** → **Render** | Variations, behaviour, underlying primitives |
| Primitive | Purpose → Preview → Install → API / explicit values | Composition, used-by Interfaces, a11y |
| Block | Purpose → Preview → composition recipe | Optional Code / file map |

```md
<!-- ✅ GOOD — Interface MDX shape -->
## Purpose
…
## Installation
`pnpm dlx shadcn@latest add https://…/r/….json`
## Getting the data
…tfl-ts + normalised shape…
## Render
`<TubeStatusBoard data={data} />`
## Variations
…labeled live states preferred over code-only…

<!-- ❌ BAD -->
## Implementation notes
## History
## Every prop in essay form before a working render path
```

### Variant galleries

Prefer **labeled live previews** (domain filters, layouts, severity states) over walls of code-only variants. Match the spirit of shadcn Button variant sections: see it, then View Code if needed.

## Agent-ready writing

Docs are read by humans **and** coding agents.

- Keep install command, normalised shape, and render snippet **short and copyable** near the top of the path.
- Prefer concrete APIs (`line.getStatus`, `TubeStatusBoard`, `data` prop) over abstract essays.
- Cross-link layers (Interface ↔ Primitive ↔ Foundations ↔ Maps) instead of duplicating trees.
- State licensing / trademark constraints early on Foundations / identity pages.

### TfL API design learning (what goes where)

The Unified API is full of traps. Teach the ones that change what a consumer **fetches or renders**. Investigation notes stay in tfl-ts.

| Audience | Place | Include | Leave out |
|---|---|---|---|
| Someone installing a board | Interface MDX, under **Getting the data** | One concrete gotcha + the `tfl-ts` call that avoids it | Hub generator, crawl, topology essays |
| Agent in this repo | Short `.cursor/rules` + pointer to the tfl-ts skill | Hard invariant (do / don't) | Restating the skill |
| tfl-ts consumers | tfl-ts `SKILL.md` + CHANGELOG | Traps table, ids, empty-array behaviour | How this site's Board URL encodes stops |

Rule of thumb: if a reader who copies the snippet would still poll the wrong StopPoint or paint `Unknown`, the page is missing a sentence. If the sentence only proves we reverse-engineered TfL, it belongs in tfl-ts.

## Nav and discovery

Navigation answers: *What is the developer trying to understand, render, or build?*

- Persistent header: **Docs · Components · Blocks · Explorer · Board** (+ Search, GitHub); logo → `/`; Docs lands on Introduction
- Docs sidebar: **Get started** + flat **Components** (preferred mode markers) + **Troubleshoot** below Components + **Primitives & Foundations** tail
- Homepage full-width (no sidebar). Blocks and Board builder: header only (no docs sidebar). `/board/view` is chromeless. Tools and Drafts: footer, development only
- Transport domains are **filters/markers**, not top-level duplicated feature trees
- Do **not** make shadcn UI atoms (Button, Dialog, Card) the product discovery path — they are chrome under `components/ui/`
- **Tools** = inspect / test / tune / debug only; otherwise Drafts or a real group
- **Maps**: Geographic vs Schematic/TubeMap as Components entries — never under Tools
- **Drafts**: footer / contributor — not permanent sidebar

## Anti-patterns

- Homepage that could belong to any design-system SaaS after removing the roundel  
- Catalog or “all components” grid as the first meaningful viewport  
- Blocks that are just another component docs page with no composition story  
- Leading Interface docs with primitive assembly before GET DATA → RENDER works  
- Fetch-inside reusable boards as the documented library API (see open-code rule)  
- Silently editing frozen IA docs to match current folders  
